cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Toporia in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Toporia: An open platform for topology optimization research"
version: 0.1.0-alpha
date-released: 2025-06-22
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/toporia/toporia

keywords:
  - topology optimization
  - structural optimization
  - finite element analysis
  - density filter
  - level-set method
  - manufacturing constraints
  - open source
  - Python

authors:
  - family-names: "Fieber"
    given-names: "Johannes"
    affiliation: "TU Delft - Delft University of Technology"

abstract: >
  Toporia is an open-source Python platform for topology optimization research.
  It provides a modular backbone with swappable filters, optimizers, and problem
  definitions, implementing methods from the research literature including
  density-based SIMP optimization, RBF level-set methods, and manufacturing
  constraint filters for milling and additive manufacturing.

